<title>SPAIN: Spain had 14.2 bln pta April current a/c surplus.</title>
<headline>Spain had 14.2 bln pta April current a/c surplus.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain gave the following figures (in billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> BALANCE OF PAYMENTS		APR 97    MAR 97     APR 96</p>
<p>  C/A balance			  14.2	25.3	 -54.1</p>
<p>  Trade balance		    -208.3     -58.9	-192.4</p>
<p>  Services			    229.3     180.8	 176.5</p>
<p>  Net tourism receipts	    259.0     197.2	 214.2</p>
<p>  Other services		    -29.7     -16.4	 -37.7</p>
<p>  Dividend income		   -46.3     -93.3	 -47.7</p>
<p>  Transfers			    39.6	-3.3	   9.5</p>
<p>  CAPITAL ACCOUNT		    76.8	71.0	 19.2</p>
<p>  FINANCIAL ACCOUNT		 -94.5	15.6	 46.0</p>
<p>  Spanish investment abroad    -178.2    -345.3     -133.0</p>
<p>  Foreign investment in Spain   459.3    -336.3     -124.9</p>
<p>  Spanish loans,deposits abroad 563.5     172.7	419.4</p>
<p>  Foreign loans, deps in Spain -797.3     577.3	456.2</p>
<p>  Movement of reserves	   -141.8     -52.8     -571.8</p>
<p>NOTE: The Bank of Spain said latest figures were provisional.</p>
<p>Non-classified element (errors and omissions) in latest capital account figures is positive for 3.5 billion pesetas. The financial account category was introduced in January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
